ation": "Department of Computer Science and Engineering, B V Raju Institute of Technology, Narsapur, Medak, 502313 Telangana India."}]}}, {"fullName": "Dhamercherla S", "lastName": "Dhamercherla", "firstName": "Swetha", "initials": "S", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Computer Science and Engineering, B V Raju Institute of Technology, Narsapur, Medak, 502313 Telangana India."}]}}, {"fullName": "Jadav SS", "lastName": "Jadav", "firstName": "Surender Singh", "initials": "SS", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5397-8956"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Centre for Molecular Cancer Research (CMCR) and Vishnu Institute of Pharmaceutical Education and Research (VIPER), Narsapur, Medak, 502313 Telangana India."}]}}, {"fullName": "Babu CM", "lastName": "Babu", "firstName": "Ch Madhu", "initials": "CM", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Computer Science and Engineering, B V Raju Institute of Technology, Narsapur, Medak, 502313 Telangana India."}]}}, {"fullName": "Ahsan MJ", "lastName": "Ahsan", "firstName": "Mohamed Jawed", "initials": "MJ", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6919-5489"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Pharmaceutical Chemistry, Maharishi Arvind College of Pharmacy, Jaipur, 302023 Rajasthan India."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-1626-8701"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5397-8956"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6919-5489"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-1742-6473"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "3", "volume": "55", "journalIssueId": 3337090, "dateOfPublication": "2022 ", "monthOfPublication": 0, "yearOfPublication": 2022, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Artif Intell Rev", "title": "Artificial intelligence review", "essn": "1573-7462", "issn": "0269-2821", "nlmid": "9883087", "isoabbreviation": "Artif Intell Rev"}, "printPublicationDate": "2022-01-01"}, "pubYear": "2022", "pageInfo": "1947-1999", "abstractText": "This review provides the feasible literature on drug discovery through ML tools and techniques that are enforced in every phase of drug development to accelerate the research process and deduce the risk and expenditure in clinical trials. Machine learning techniques improve the decision-making in pharmaceutical data across various applications like QSAR analysis, hit discoveries, de novo drug architectures to retrieve accurate outcomes. Target validation, prognostic biomarkers, digital pathology are considered under problem statements in this review. ML challenges must be applicable for the main cause of inadequacy in interpretability outcomes that may restrict the applications in drug discovery. In clinical trials, absolute and methodological data must be generated to tackle many puzzles in validating ML techniques, improving decision-making, promoting awareness in ML approaches, and deducing risk failures in drug discovery.", "affiliation": "Department of Computer Science and Engineering, B V Raju Institute of Technology, Narsapur, Medak, 502313 Telangana India.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Journal Article"]}, "keywordList": {"keyword": ["Artificial intelligence", "drug discovery", "Machine Learning", "Target Validation", "Digital Pathology", "Prognostic Biomarkers"]}, "fullTextUrlList": {"fullTextUrl": [{"availability": "Subscription required", "availabilityCode": "S", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10462-021-10058-4"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC8356896"}, {"availability": "